---
description: Every card or panel on a screen (web and Android) must be a draggable, resizable board
alwaysApply: true
---

# Every board is draggable

Any card, panel or widget shown on a page or screen is a **board**: the person can press it and drag it to a new
place, and where it lands is saved. Never add a fixed, unmovable card.

## Web (`src/features/<page>/`)

Put each card in a `<Panel>` inside the page's `<Board>` (`src/components/Board.tsx`). Do not render a bare
`.card` / `<section>` straight into the page.

```tsx
// BAD: a card that can't be moved
<section className="card">...</section>

// GOOD: a panel, with a stable id the saved layout remembers
<Board page="goals" editing={layout.editing} onEditingChange={layout.setEditing}>
  <Panel id="overview" title="Active goals" size="third">
    <div className="card">...</div>
  </Panel>
  {goals.map((g) => (
    <Panel key={g.id} id={`goal:${g.id}`} title={g.title} size="full">...</Panel>
  ))}
</Board>
```

- Give the page a `PanelFilter` and a `SettingsMenu` with `useLayoutEditing().item` in its header.
- A panel `id` never changes (it is saved). Per-item panels use `kind:${id}`.
- Sizes are only `third | half | threeQuarters | full`.
- Only short-lived things (an open "add" form, a modal, filters, the page header) may sit outside a Board.

## Android (`android/.../phone/*Screen.kt`)

Mark every card with `.board("stable-id")` (or build it with `panel(title, ..., id = ...)`), and call
`arrange("phone-<screen>", content)` after the container is filled. The person holds a card to drag it.

```kotlin
content.addView(summaryCard(today).board("summary"))
shown.forEach { content.addView(goalCard(it, today).board("goal:${it.id}")) }
arrange("phone-goals", content)
```

## Every new screen

When adding a new tab, make its cards boards on both web and phone before calling it done, and say so in the README.